    {
      "id": "claim_23c9ca8aeafd4fd695579dc1cdb58a96",
      "statement": "After precommit passes, the packaging phase runs the zero-token deterministic anti-slop gate (run_deterministic_slop_gate in dispatcher/slop_gate.py, wired in as the package.slop_gate step of _package_and_open_pr before commit, with target_branch, spec_text, and skip_untested_check): it errors on leftover debugger statements (breakpoint(), pdb.set_trace(), import pdb, debugger;), unresolved TODO/FIXME/XXX/HACK placeholder comments, skipped tests, assertion-free newly added test functions (assertion_free_test), production code adding more than 20 net lines without any test lines (untested_production_diff, DEFAULT_UNTESTED_PROD_LINE_THRESHOLD=20, skippable via ZEROFACTORY_SKIP_UNTESTED_CHECK or per-task skip_untested_check), and modifications of files named in the spec's Do Not Touch / Non-Goals section (do_not_touch_violation); the net-line budget (diff_budget_exceeded) defaults to DEFAULT_MAX_DIFF_LINES=800 and is overridden by ZEROFACTORY_MAX_DIFF_LINES (<=0 disables); large diffs, net test-line deletions, dependency-manifest changes, new lint/type suppressors, and mock-heavy test additions (mock_heavy_test) are warnings; its compact diff-hygiene scorecard (build_diff_hygiene_scorecard) is pre-digested into the zf-reviewer prompt so review starts from a quantitative diff summary.",
